  "text": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Basel Framework: NSF30.32 FAQ1 (footnote number)",
      "summary": "The NSF30.32 FAQ attributes the definition of NSFR derivative liabilities to footnote 18, which holds the RSF formula; the definition is in footnote 2.",
      "impact": "Position: Reader follows the FAQ to footnote 18 for NSFR derivative liabilities Reading a: Footnote 18 gives only RSF = 100% x MAX(A - L, 0), no deduction of VM Reading b: Footnote 2 / NSF30.9 gives L = derivative liabilities - VM posted Difference: definition not found by pointer",
      "correction": "Clarify or correct the cited passage so that the rule and its references give one result for the stated case."
    }
  },
